---
# Copy to .pi/agents/<name>.md (project, trusted only) or ~/.pi/agent/agents/<name>.md (user).
# `name` and `description` are required; a file missing either is silently skipped.
# Reusing a built-in's name (reviewer, researcher, planner, oracle, worker) overrides it.
name: my-role
description: "One line - what this role is for (shown in /swarm agents)"
# Tool allowlist, comma list or YAML list. Read-only: read, grep, find, ls
# (bash runs checks but can also write). Writing: add edit, write.
# Omit to fall back to workerTools in swarm.json, then pi's defaults.
tools: read, grep, find, ls
# lead | worker | cheap — picks models.<tier> from swarm.json. Omitted: cheap if all tools are read-only, else worker.
tier: cheap
# model: provider/model   # optional; beats tier
---
System prompt goes here. Say what the role does, what it must not do,
and what the final reply must contain.
